WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.980
SpaceX cut falcon 9 pad turn around to 32 hours, beating the 45 hour record and freeing pad capacity. This is SpaceX Daily, episode 171. Dragon splash down with station samples, xai's Memphis cooling paws, and starlink's block in China, plus an engineering deep dive on chamber pressure. SpaceX sent the classified NRL 136 payload for the National Reconnaissance Office, or NRO, off Vandenberg Space Force Base Launch Complex 4E.

00:00:29.980 --> 00:00:36.920
at 4.23 in the morning local time on November 22nd. Technology.org reports, three minutes

00:00:36.920 --> 00:00:44.220
and 21 seconds past the new pad mark. Booster B1097 completed its 14th flight. It separated

00:00:44.220 --> 00:00:48.980
about two minutes after leaving the pad and landed at Landing Zone 4, roughly seven

00:00:48.980 --> 00:00:54.040
and a half minutes after liftoff, back at the launch base. SpaceX Vice President of

00:00:54.040 --> 00:00:59.080
Launch Kiko Donchev credited the West Coast team and posted that preparations finished several

00:00:59.080 --> 00:01:02.880
hours ahead of schedule, with the next target a 24-hour turnaround.

00:01:03.580 --> 00:01:09.900
The flight was the NRO's sixth of 2026, and the 15th supporting its proliferated architecture

00:01:09.900 --> 00:01:10.800
satellite network.

00:01:11.240 --> 00:01:16.940
And every one of those six NRO missions this year flew on Falcon 9, with classified payloads

00:01:16.940 --> 00:01:18.040
into low-earth orbit.

00:01:18.500 --> 00:01:23.320
The proliferated design flies many small satellites in low-earth orbit, so they can

00:01:23.320 --> 00:01:26.760
take turns watching a location and stand in if another fails.

00:01:26.760 --> 00:01:32.480
And the NRO has not disclosed how many satellites flew on this mission or their technical details.

00:01:32.760 --> 00:01:41.880
The NRO began deploying the constellation in May, 2024, with NRO-L146, NRO-L179 launched

00:01:41.880 --> 00:01:48.500
on June 19, 2026, and the previous pad turnaround mark had been set at Cape Canaveral Pad 40.

00:01:49.366 --> 00:01:56.206
An uncrewed dragon, SpaceCue reports, splashed down off California on November 21, with biology

00:01:56.206 --> 00:02:00.066
collected for cancer and aging research on the International Space Station.

00:02:00.626 --> 00:02:05.886
It also carried a failed Canadarm 2 wrist joint, so engineers on the ground can inspect it,

00:02:06.226 --> 00:02:11.606
stowed by NASA astronaut Jessica Watkins after crews replaced it on a June 30th spacewalk.

00:02:12.286 --> 00:02:16.566
Whether held the capsule three days, and it left the station on November 20th.

00:02:17.340 --> 00:02:22.800
XAI stopped construction of a South Memphis wastewater recycling plant, Wise Voter Reports,

00:02:23.300 --> 00:02:25.380
and now expects to restart in January.

00:02:25.380 --> 00:02:30.340
That stoppage hits the cooling schedule the Colossus Class training cluster depends on.

00:02:31.171 --> 00:02:36.831
Starlink service Elon Musk posted is unavailable in China because the system is illegal there.

00:02:37.411 --> 00:02:42.871
Elon Musk tied Starlink's next expansion to unsupervised full-self driving, vehicles that

00:02:42.871 --> 00:02:47.111
operate without a human at the wheel, and said coverage should arrive toward the end

00:02:47.111 --> 00:02:51.871
of next year to feed the high bandwidth those cars need so passengers can work and watch

00:02:51.871 --> 00:02:52.471
entertainment.

00:02:52.471 --> 00:02:59.411
SIGI Space posted on X that Tesla full self-driving has become instantly intuitive and made driving

00:02:59.411 --> 00:03:05.862
measurably more pleasant, a personal observation rather than a company release. China put out its

00:03:05.862 --> 00:03:11.962
clearest timeline yet for putting astronauts on the moon before 2030. NASA Space Flight reports,

00:03:12.582 --> 00:03:17.702
starting with three uncrewed precursor flights. Crude flight out of Earth orbit is supposed to

00:03:17.702 --> 00:03:20.082
wait until those three robotic missions succeed.

00:03:21.166 --> 00:03:23.926
Sci-Guy Space observed that earlier NASA decisions

00:03:23.926 --> 00:03:27.186
prevented Orion from gaining low lunar orbit capability

00:03:27.186 --> 00:03:30.706
despite two decades of funding, his reading of that history

00:03:30.706 --> 00:03:32.586
rather than an agency confirmation.

00:03:33.306 --> 00:03:36.586
Rocket Lab's chief financial officer, trading view reports,

00:03:37.126 --> 00:03:39.726
noted stronger pricing power for electron launches

00:03:39.726 --> 00:03:43.266
amid reduced availability of SpaceX ride share opportunities.

00:03:43.986 --> 00:03:46.626
Electron demand remains firm even as the stock

00:03:46.626 --> 00:03:51.730
just posted its worst week on record. In the same window, a YouTube report not

00:03:51.730 --> 00:03:56.810
confirmed by the company says SpaceX is preparing booster 24 and ship 42 for

00:03:56.810 --> 00:04:02.970
Starship Flight 17, right after Flight 15, a test that could debut from Pad 39A

00:04:02.970 --> 00:04:08.490
in Florida. Cathy Wood at ARC Invest, Deal Room Notes, says Orbital Compute could

00:04:08.490 --> 00:04:12.970
undercut terrestrial data centers within two years, with Starship projected at

00:04:12.970 --> 00:04:16.890
at $358 per kilogram to orbit in 2027.

00:04:17.971 --> 00:04:21.991
Worth keeping an eye on, Lenders could block SpaceX from putting billions of dollars

00:04:21.991 --> 00:04:27.891
of advanced AI chips in orbit, because their financing covenants, MLQ reports, were written

00:04:27.891 --> 00:04:30.251
before the orbital compute strategy existed.

00:04:30.871 --> 00:04:35.271
Those terms could stop the deployment even after technical and regulatory hurdles fall.

00:04:35.911 --> 00:04:40.651
The way out is a debt renegotiation or a showing that orbital assets sit outside the current

00:04:40.651 --> 00:04:41.211
restrictions.

00:04:41.211 --> 00:04:47.731
A $74 billion AI data center plan still has to clear votes in Texas and Arizona on December

00:04:47.731 --> 00:04:48.051
9.

00:04:49.062 --> 00:04:54.122
On the AI front, Elon Musk said the price of RAM, the memory on each board, pushed the

00:04:54.122 --> 00:05:01.382
team to cut AI 4.5 hardware from 32GB to 24GB per unit because memory bandwidth already

00:05:01.382 --> 00:05:04.242
stops the larger configuration from being fully used.

00:05:04.702 --> 00:05:09.442
That cut holds the design inside practical operating limits and trims what the parts cost.

00:05:09.442 --> 00:05:14.736
chamber pressure is the subject of today's engineering deep dive, starting with

00:05:14.736 --> 00:05:20.016
the V2 engine that delivered 245 kilonewtons of sea-level thrust at only 14 to

00:05:20.016 --> 00:05:25.996
15 bar while burning liquid oxygen and 75% ethanol. Its turbo pump running on

00:05:25.996 --> 00:05:30.856
steam from hydrogen peroxide decomposition, a cycle that limited efficiency and

00:05:30.856 --> 00:05:37.696
reusability. Raptor 3 reaches 2,452 kilonewtons at sea level, roughly 10 times

00:05:37.696 --> 00:05:43.336
245 in a full-flow staged combustion cycle that routes all propellant through the turbines

00:05:43.336 --> 00:05:50.256
before the main chamber, raising pressure to 300 to 350 bar, about 20 times the V2's 15

00:05:50.256 --> 00:05:56.676
bar when you divide 300 by 15. Specific impulse, the seconds of thrust from a unit of propellant,

00:05:56.956 --> 00:06:05.276
is approximately 330 seconds at sea level and 355 in vacuum, and 330 times 9.81 meters per second

00:06:05.276 --> 00:06:09.796
squared is on the order of 3,200 meters per second of exhaust velocity.

00:06:10.336 --> 00:06:21.636
Mass stays at 1,525 kilograms, so 2,452,000 newtons divided by 1,525 times 9.81 yields a thrust

00:06:21.636 --> 00:06:23.476
to weight near 164.

00:06:24.056 --> 00:06:29.036
Higher impulse and pressure shrink the propellant fraction a rocket must carry, and full flow

00:06:29.036 --> 00:06:34.156
eliminates gas generator exhaust that dumps unburned turbine flow overboard on older cycles,

00:06:34.156 --> 00:06:37.896
vehicles, converting nearly all of the chemical energy into useful thrust.

00:06:38.476 --> 00:06:43.536
The V2's spherical chamber and 18 injector elements were state-of-the-art in 1944.

00:06:44.336 --> 00:06:49.116
Raptor uses pinto injectors and actively cooled chambers for mixing efficiency and thermal

00:06:49.116 --> 00:06:50.876
margin the V2 could not reach.

00:06:51.436 --> 00:06:56.296
33 of those engines on the super-heavy booster lift a vehicle whose dry mass is only a few

00:06:56.296 --> 00:07:00.796
percent of its propellant load, then return that super-heavy booster for reuse within

00:07:00.796 --> 00:07:04.896
in hours, extending the physics to a vehicle in order of magnitude larger.

